WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.370 --> 00:00:06.500
Entanglement is often blamed for all the spooky
weirdness of quantum mechanics.

00:00:06.500 --> 00:00:11.330
In this video I’ll explain what it really
is and one of the coolest consequences: the

00:00:11.330 --> 00:00:12.520
EPR paradox.

00:00:12.520 --> 00:00:17.362
If you haven’t watched any of my other videos
on quantum mechanics, you might want to watch

00:00:17.362 --> 00:00:22.880
these two- but I’ll have a really quick
recap for everyone’s benefit

00:00:22.880 --> 00:00:26.849
There are only 2 quantum rules we need to
give us entanglement.

00:00:26.849 --> 00:00:28.980
The first is the superposition rule.

00:00:28.980 --> 00:00:33.670
It says, if there are several options for
an object and if there is no way anything

00:00:33.670 --> 00:00:39.649
can know which option the object is doing,
we say it is in a superposition of doing all

00:00:39.649 --> 00:00:40.649
of them.

00:00:40.649 --> 00:00:46.710
Now, importantly, this is very different from
saying it is doing one or the other, but we

00:00:46.710 --> 00:00:48.230
don’t know which.

00:00:48.230 --> 00:00:52.809
For example: If you flipped a coin, you may
not know whether it’s heads or tails- but

00:00:52.809 --> 00:00:55.739
this doesn’t mean it’s in a superposition.

00:00:55.739 --> 00:00:59.749
You know it’s one or the other, but you’re
not sure which.

00:00:59.749 --> 00:01:05.870
A superposition is a state where a particle
seems to really do both at the same time-

00:01:05.870 --> 00:01:09.690
at least in some interpretations.

00:01:09.690 --> 00:01:14.480
Then there’s the measurement rule: that
if you measure a particle that’s in a superposition,

00:01:14.480 --> 00:01:18.190
it must collapse to just one of the options
in the superposition.

00:01:18.190 --> 00:01:22.520
Here’s how all of this can naturally lead
to entanglement.

00:01:22.520 --> 00:01:26.690
We’ll take an example using spin- but if
you don’t know what that is, don’t worry

00:01:26.690 --> 00:01:27.690
too much.

00:01:27.690 --> 00:01:31.510
Imagine we have a very energetic particle
of light.

00:01:31.510 --> 00:01:37.360
Then, using einstein’s famous formula, it
can convert that energy into mass- for example,

00:01:37.360 --> 00:01:39.980
it could form two new particles.

00:01:39.980 --> 00:01:43.910
But there are a bunch of conservation laws
in physics that restrict what these particles

00:01:43.910 --> 00:01:45.920
are and what they do.

00:01:45.920 --> 00:01:52.760
For example, a photon has no electrical charge,
so these new particles should have no charge-

00:01:52.760 --> 00:01:54.140
in total.

00:01:54.140 --> 00:02:00.650
So one could be an electron, and the other
a positive version of an electron- a positron,

00:02:00.650 --> 00:02:03.000
then in total, there charge is 0.

00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:07.530
But there’s also a thing called conservation
of spin.

00:02:07.530 --> 00:02:12.510
Photons never have any spin, but both electrons
and positrons do.

00:02:12.510 --> 00:02:16.840
They can either have spin up, which is positive,
or spin down, which is negative.

00:02:16.840 --> 00:02:21.829
So for their total spin to cancel, one should
be up, the other down.

00:02:21.829 --> 00:02:24.349
But which is which?

00:02:24.349 --> 00:02:28.180
Usually you’d want to say, it is one of
these ways, but you don’t know which.

00:02:28.180 --> 00:02:34.099
However, remember in quantum mechanics, if
there’s no way to know, it must be a superposition

00:02:34.099 --> 00:02:35.239
of both.

00:02:35.239 --> 00:02:42.019
This state is entangled- but you may not see
what’s so special about it yet.

00:02:42.019 --> 00:02:46.689
Entanglement is the crazy property that it’s
impossible to describe the state of one of

00:02:46.689 --> 00:02:49.379
these particles without the other.

00:02:49.379 --> 00:02:54.299
To see what this means and why this is unique
to quantum mechanics let’s compare it to

00:02:54.299 --> 00:02:56.140
the not quantum scenario.

00:02:56.140 --> 00:03:01.641
Classically, we’d think it has to be one
or the other of these cases- and not both,

00:03:01.641 --> 00:03:04.590
but we don’t know which.

00:03:04.590 --> 00:03:09.900
Here if I wanted to describe the state of
the electron, it’d be up if the positron

00:03:09.900 --> 00:03:13.019
is down, and down if the positron is up.

00:03:13.019 --> 00:03:18.101
This... seems like it fits my definition of
entanglement: it’s impossible to describe

00:03:18.101 --> 00:03:21.769
the state of the electron without talking
about the positron.

00:03:21.769 --> 00:03:23.730
So is this entanglement?

00:03:23.730 --> 00:03:24.730
Well actually, no.

00:03:24.730 --> 00:03:29.510
Because really, the particles are doing one
thing, say this one.

00:03:29.510 --> 00:03:32.870
If I knew that, I could say the electron is
up.

00:03:32.870 --> 00:03:37.659
It’s only because I didn’t know which
case it was that I described them like this.

00:03:37.659 --> 00:03:40.830
But in the quantum case, there isn’t this
way out.

00:03:40.830 --> 00:03:46.220
The particles are apparently doing both these
things, and so, there isn’t an actual state

00:03:46.220 --> 00:03:51.370
of the electron we can talk about- the electron
is not actually just up.

00:03:51.370 --> 00:03:56.520
It’s both up if the other is down and down
if the other is up.

00:03:56.520 --> 00:04:01.400
You can never talk about the state of these
particles seperately, only their joint state.

00:04:01.400 --> 00:04:02.700
That’s entanglement.

00:04:02.700 --> 00:04:04.950
But you might have an objection to this.

00:04:04.950 --> 00:04:10.299
Can’t you say, the electron’s state is
a superposition of up and down?

00:04:10.299 --> 00:04:14.659
Well there are two ways to show that that
isn’t the state of the electron.

00:04:14.659 --> 00:04:19.340
The first is just mathematically showing these
two states aren’t equal, but that’s a

00:04:19.340 --> 00:04:20.340
bit boring.

00:04:20.340 --> 00:04:25.360
Instead, let’s see that this would lead
to a contradiction.

00:04:25.360 --> 00:04:28.630
Suppose Alice takes the electron and Bob takes
the positron.

00:04:28.630 --> 00:04:34.539
We’ll assume that the state of Alice’s
particle is a superposition of up and down,

00:04:34.539 --> 00:04:37.280
and the same for Bob’s particle.

00:04:37.280 --> 00:04:43.150
If this is actually true, then this lets us
describe the state of each particle seperately,

00:04:43.150 --> 00:04:45.020
without mentioning the other one.

00:04:45.020 --> 00:04:52.600
Then say Alice measures hers and finds it
to be up, so her state collapses, but Bob’s

00:04:52.600 --> 00:04:53.600
doesn’t.

00:04:53.600 --> 00:04:57.920
He can measure his, and get up too.

00:04:57.920 --> 00:05:03.060
This means they started with a photon with
zero spin, and got two particles with positive

00:05:03.060 --> 00:05:05.720
spin- which breaks conservation.

00:05:05.720 --> 00:05:12.010
So no, the total state can’t be written
as two individual states.

00:05:12.010 --> 00:05:14.729
The real state is this combination.

00:05:14.729 --> 00:05:20.300
And what really happens is, Alice measures
hers, and say gets up.

00:05:20.300 --> 00:05:24.509
Then that collapses the superposition to just
this bit.

00:05:24.509 --> 00:05:30.560
So Bob will definitely measure down, and it
total the spin is conserved.

00:05:30.560 --> 00:05:35.770
So we see that we have to believe the particles
are entangled to explain this.

00:05:35.770 --> 00:05:41.419
It was Einstein though who realised the extraordinary
consequence of entanglement- and it’s very

00:05:41.419 --> 00:05:42.419
simple.

00:05:42.419 --> 00:05:48.919
Let’s get Alice and Bob to go very far away
from each other, and do the same experiment.

00:05:48.919 --> 00:05:54.441
Notice something, Alice’s measurement of
her particle effects Bob’s particle, because

00:05:54.441 --> 00:05:57.240
it has to be opposite.

00:05:57.240 --> 00:06:03.120
Even worse, that effect has to be instant,
because if Bob measures his particle a split

00:06:03.120 --> 00:06:09.909
second after Alice he still needs to get the
opposite result- so there can’t be any delay

00:06:09.909 --> 00:06:16.039
in how quickly Alice’s measurement effects
Bob’s; Somehow the message from Alice’s

00:06:16.039 --> 00:06:19.639
electron to the positron travelled instantly.

00:06:19.639 --> 00:06:23.610
In other words, this effect is nonlocal.

00:06:23.610 --> 00:06:28.669
The issue is, this seems to contradict Einstein’s
theory of relativity.

00:06:28.669 --> 00:06:32.389
In that theory, no information can travel
faster than light.

00:06:32.389 --> 00:06:35.819
The reason is that, if you could send a message
faster than light than you could cause things

00:06:35.819 --> 00:06:39.310
like time travel and the grandfather paradox.

00:06:39.310 --> 00:06:44.610
Einstein thought this would be enough to convince
people that Quantum theory is silly... but

00:06:44.610 --> 00:06:49.030
what really happened was the scientific community
of the time weren’t able to come up with

00:06:49.030 --> 00:06:53.750
a good answer to it, and decided to ignore
it.

00:06:53.750 --> 00:06:58.159
It was wasn’t until much later that people
cared, and even later that it was proved that

00:06:58.159 --> 00:07:02.689
the sort of spooky action at a distance in
quantum mechanics has doesn’t allow time

00:07:02.689 --> 00:07:08.970
paradoxes- since Alice can never send any
message to bob through this.

00:07:08.970 --> 00:07:14.319
But partly because of the nonlocality in quantum
mechanics, it still doesn’t sit very uncomfortably

00:07:14.319 --> 00:07:17.460
with relativity.

00:07:17.460 --> 00:07:19.430
Thanks for watching this video!

00:07:19.430 --> 00:07:23.379
So here are some homework questions for you
to try and answer in the comments.

00:07:23.379 --> 00:07:28.460
1 Explain why Alice can never send any messages
through this set up.

00:07:28.460 --> 00:07:34.210
2 This is one to practice working with wavefunctions
of several objects.

00:07:34.210 --> 00:07:38.810
Prove mathematically that it’s impossible
to write our state as two separate states

00:07:38.810 --> 00:07:40.570
for the electron and positron

00:07:40.570 --> 00:07:45.540
3 this one is very relevant to quantum computing.

00:07:45.540 --> 00:07:51.620
If you have just one electron or positron,
you only need 2 numbers to describe its state.

00:07:51.620 --> 00:07:53.830
Now suppose you have n of them.

00:07:53.830 --> 00:08:00.159
If they are not entangled, how many numbers
to you need to describe the state?

00:08:00.159 --> 00:08:03.389
What about for a general state that is allowed
to be entangled?

